  "hostNotes": "TRAP: Totti's Lorne serves no pizza. The famous 'pizza oven' bakes the puffy wood-fired flatbread (~$16) that diners pile antipasti onto, and a 3AW review notes the table liking that there was no pizza on the menu. Grade generously: accept anything on the Totti's antipasti list (confirmed at Lorne: prosciutto, burrata, kingfish crudo, melon; Totti's staples elsewhere: olives, salami, anchovies, mortadella, stracciatella, 'nduja, sardines, octopus, pickled veg) plus any plausible pizza topping, merge spellings per the aliases, and treat 'there's no pizza / it's the bread' as a correct deep cut worth the top rarity, not a dodge. Reject pastas and mains (pappardelle lamb ragu, ziti prawn alla vodka, King George whiting, lamb chop) as non-toppings. Local traps: Lorne's actual pizzeria is Pizza Pizza on Mountjoy Parade, and Merivale's real pizza spin-off is Oti' (Roman slabs) in Sydney."
}
